From db1da78955efc99d3908b9d8720a0a662efc1a06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khunmax2 <khuncharoenmax1@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:23:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Make the container build reproducible off a clean checkout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two fixes that a `docker build` needs and that upstream's files do not have.
Written by the repository owner while getting the image to build at all; kept
here as a patch for the same reason as the others — so the OpenMAIC checkout
stays a pristine mirror and this survives a re-clone.

.dockerignore — Docker matches patterns from the context root only, not at
every level the way .gitignore does, so a pnpm workspace needs explicit `**`
globs for its nested copies. Without them, and specifically on a Windows host,
pnpm's nested `node_modules` are absolute `D:/...` symlinks: they are copied
into the image, are dead there, and shadow the real ones the deps stage built.
`**/dist` is the same story for package build output, which the deps stage
postinstall regenerates anyway.

Dockerfile — `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRO_WORKBENCH_ENABLED` was the one build-time flag in
this family with no matching ARG/ENV pair, so it could not be set at build time
like its neighbours. Next inlines `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` at build, so a runtime
environment variable does not reach the browser bundle; the ARG is the only way.

Both are upstream candidates: neither mentions DeepTutor, and the .dockerignore
one is a plain bug for anyone building on Windows.
---
 integration/maic/.dockerignore | 8 ++++++++
 integration/maic/Dockerfile    | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/integration/maic/.dockerignore b/integration/maic/.dockerignore
index 9caa957a6..9c8558eee 100644
--- a/integration/maic/.dockerignore
+++ b/integration/maic/.dockerignore
@@ -1,12 +1,20 @@
 # dependencies
+# Docker matches .dockerignore patterns from the context root, not at every
+# level like .gitignore, so the nested workspace copies need explicit globs.
+# On a Windows host pnpm writes them as absolute D:/... symlinks, which are
+# dead inside the container and shadow the ones the deps stage built.
 node_modules
+**/node_modules
 .pnpm-store
 
 # build output
+# Package dist/ is rebuilt by the deps stage postinstall; copying the host copy
+# only risks staleness.
 .next
 out
 build
 dist
+**/dist
 
 # git
 .git
diff --git a/integration/maic/Dockerfile b/integration/maic/Dockerfile
index c326ae627..d4faad060 100644
--- a/integration/maic/Dockerfile
+++ b/integration/maic/Dockerfile
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ FROM base AS builder
 ARG ALLOWED_FRAME_ANCESTORS
 ARG NEXT_PUBLIC_PERSISTENCE
 ARG NEXT_PUBLIC_PERSISTENCE_TOKEN
+ARG NEXT_PUBLIC_PRO_WORKBENCH_ENABLED
 ARG NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_EDITOR_ENABLED
 ARG NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_EDITOR_RENDERER_ENABLED
 ARG NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_PLAYBACK_RENDERER_ENABLED
@@ -62,6 +63,7 @@ ARG NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_PPTX_IMPORT
 ENV ALLOWED_FRAME_ANCESTORS=$ALLOWED_FRAME_ANCESTORS
 ENV NEXT_PUBLIC_PERSISTENCE=$NEXT_PUBLIC_PERSISTENCE
 ENV NEXT_PUBLIC_PERSISTENCE_TOKEN=$NEXT_PUBLIC_PERSISTENCE_TOKEN
+ENV NEXT_PUBLIC_PRO_WORKBENCH_ENABLED=$NEXT_PUBLIC_PRO_WORKBENCH_ENABLED
 ENV NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_EDITOR_ENABLED=$NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_EDITOR_ENABLED
 ENV NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_EDITOR_RENDERER_ENABLED=$NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_EDITOR_RENDERER_ENABLED
 ENV NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_PLAYBACK_RENDERER_ENABLED=$NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_PLAYBACK_RENDERER_ENABLED
-- 
2.51.0.windows.2

